1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,321
This is a fresh local Canton sandbox. One operator switches roles with

2
00:00:06,321 --> 00:00:11,641
authentication disabled. Assets are simulated, with no external backing. A trusted issuer

3
00:00:11,641 --> 00:00:16,519
controls issuance. Reset reseeds the demo at a price of one.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,470
The lender reserves one hundred simulated USDC. Terms are five interest and

5
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:31,940
one hundred fifty collateral units. At price one, loan-to-value is sixty-six point

6
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:37,410
seven percent, below ninety. The offer records its funded principal and ledger

7
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:37,866
offset.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,059
The borrower accepts. Canton consumes the offer, locks one hundred fifty collateral

9
00:00:49,059 --> 00:00:55,118
units, and delivers one hundred simulated USDC. The fifty-unit reserve stays separate.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,632
Outsider is not a stakeholder. Their party-scoped query returns zero contracts and

11
00:01:04,632 --> 00:01:06,040
literally empty brackets.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,478
Valuer publishes a manual zero point sixty-two mark on the same stream.

13
00:01:13,478 --> 00:01:17,957
It is simulated data in this demo, not a live oracle; the

14
00:01:17,957 --> 00:01:19,823
loan stays outside that view.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,477
At zero point sixty-two, value is ninety-three and loan-to-value about one hundred

16
00:01:30,477 --> 00:01:34,584
seven point five percent. Lender opens a sixty-second call.

17
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,359
Before deadline, borrower uses exact fifty-unit reserve. Canton consumes it, replaces the

18
00:01:42,359 --> 00:01:47,717
loan with two hundred locked units, clears the call, and restores loan-to-value

19
00:01:47,717 --> 00:01:53,076
to about eighty point six percent before maturity. Main path does not

20
00:01:53,076 --> 00:01:53,522
wait.

21
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:02,248
Borrower repays exactly one hundred five: one hundred principal plus five interest.

22
00:02:02,248 --> 00:02:07,496
Loan closes Repaid, two hundred collateral units are released to the borrower,

23
00:02:07,496 --> 00:02:10,120
and lender receives one hundred five.

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,110
The regulator inspects the closed deal but has no action button. The

25
00:02:18,110 --> 00:02:23,220
valuer sees valuation records, not the loan. The issuer remains a trusted

26
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:28,330
stakeholder in simulated inventory and lifecycle records. That visibility is deliberate in

27
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:29,181
this demo.

28
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,330
The activity feed records transaction IDs, synchronizer IDs, and created or archived

29
00:02:40,330 --> 00:02:45,661
contracts. The raw ledger view separately shows the party's active contracts. Final

30
00:02:45,661 --> 00:02:50,991
state is Repaid: two hundred units returned and one hundred five paid.

31
00:02:50,991 --> 00:02:56,322
This is a local demo, not external settlement or an independent audit.
